phis (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: config/phis-runtime.json, which holds the database passwords and the API tokens, is
    written with mode 0600. Every write replaced it with a file carrying the umask's mode (usually
    0644), so it was world-readable after db bootstrap, the setup pages or any CLI command that writes
    the configuration, even after a chmod by hand. postinst sets 0600 on every configure, which corrects
    an existing stage on upgrade.

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:43:25 +0000

phis (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: released for Debian 13 (trixie) and Ubuntu 24.04 (noble), on amd64 and arm64, through
    the apt repository on apt.phisys.com (channel testing); each distribution carries its own version,
    <version>+<distribution>.
  * INSTALL: the Debian package installs from apt.phisys.com; Node 24 comes from NodeSource.

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:18:50 +0000

phis (0.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Payments: a Provider may complete the price with tax, shipping and discounts. Core validates the
    pricing policy at create, filters methods by their pricing features, checks totals on every
    Observation, freezes the total at authorisation or capture and carries additions on refunds. The
    payments table's CHECKs changed (a `pricing` object, captured up to the validated total): an
    existing database needs them replaced by hand, `schema apply` does not alter them.
  * notifications:v1 for Add-ons: occasions declared in the manifest, notify() reaches a Site member or
    a contact; Core renders salutation, frame and Site link and sends through the outbox.
  * Built against @phis/contracts 0.7.0.

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000

phis (0.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * deepl.formality (prefer_more or prefer_less) asks DeepL for one address form, so a store shared by
    every Site no longer mixes German Sie and du. It is part of the translation fingerprint, so Sites
    drop translations they kept from before a change.
  * The setup page links the phis-dev organisation and names the Apache License 2.0; the default
    sender name is phis.

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:24:15 +0000

phis (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The server's external package links (pg, argon2, sharp) resolve to the packaged node_modules; 0.2.0
    to 0.2.2 failed their first start with "Cannot find package 'pg-<hash>'". The package build now
    fails on a link that leads nowhere.

